# Line endings: every text file is stored and checked out with LF on every OS, so Windows tools (VS Code, Git's
# autocrlf, formatters) can never make files look "changed" – that is what blocked `git pull` before.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Packages and images are binary; the unpacked extension must stay byte-identical on every OS.
*.vsix binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.mp4 binary
dist/vscode-extension/** -text
